Tools available to the ceiling-fixture designer. Field names, types, enums, ranges strictly enforced.

# Asset generation

- generate_ceiling_assets(object_descriptions: list[str], short_names: list[str], desired_dimensions: list[[w,d,h]], style_context: str = "") -> {success, assets: [{object_id, width, depth, height}]}
  Batch-generate ceiling-mounted assets. All three list args MUST have equal length.
  desired_dimensions: [width, depth, height], where height = hang distance below ceiling.

# Placement

- place_ceiling_object(asset_id: str, position_x: float, position_y: float, rotation_degrees: float = 0.0) -> Result
  Place an asset on the ceiling plane.
    position_x / position_y: meters in room coordinates (NOT wall-local).
    rotation_degrees: rotation around Z axis.
  asset_id MUST be an object_id returned by an earlier generate_ceiling_assets.
  MUST be within room_bounds; object's top is automatically flush with ceiling.

# Correction

- move_ceiling_object(object_id: str, position_x: float, position_y: float, rotation_degrees: float = 0.0) -> Result

- remove_ceiling_object(object_id: str) -> Result

- rescale_ceiling_object(object_id: str, scale_factor: float) -> Result
  scale_factor > 0 and != 1.0. Affects all instances of the asset.

# Validation

- check_physics() -> str
  Run the physics/collision check after placement or correction. Use its
  result to detect ceiling-object penetration and other scene collisions.

# Strict rules

- position_x / position_y are in room XY (same frame as furniture), NOT wall-local.
- Z is implicit: the object hangs from the ceiling; don't try to pass z.
- asset_id values must match those produced by generate_ceiling_assets exactly, postfixes included.
